  "sort": 0,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You call forth the spirit of a Construct. It appears in an unoccupied space you can see within range and uses the Construct Spirit stat block. When you cast the spell, choose a material: Clay, Metal, or Stone. The creature looks like an animate statue of that material (you choose its appearance), which determines some details of its stat block. It disappears when it drops to 0 Hit Points or when the spell ends.</p><p>The creature is an ally to you and your allies. In combat, it shares your Initiative count but takes its turn immediately after yours. It obeys your verbal commands (no action required by you); if you give none, it takes the Dodge action and uses its movement to avoid danger.</p><p><strong>Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.</strong> Use the spell slot’s level for the spell’s level in the stat block.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-WYad6EcmJi7Cl2VN\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Summon asks for the material. The spirit’s AC, Hit Points and Slam damage include the spell’s level, and Stony Lethargy uses your spell save DC.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
